MUST be recorded as a regression note and requires a\nconstitution amendment first.\n\nRationale: cachetools is a published library; downstream code depends on\nstable, predictable semantics.\n\n### II. Testable Acceptance Criteria\n\nEvery requirement MUST state observable, testable acceptance criteria\nbefore implementation starts. Each criterion MUST name the inputs, the\nexpected observable outcome (return value, raised exception, or state\nafter the operation), and any state-preservation guarantees (for\nexample, rejecting invalid input MUST leave prior value, tags, and\nrecency unchanged). A requirement that cannot be expressed as a\nfailing-then-passing test MUST be rewritten or deferred, not implemented\non assumption.\n\nRationale: testable criteria make completion verifiable and keep scope\nhonest.\n\n### III. Evidence Over Assertion\n\nClaims about behavior MUST distinguish observed evidence from unverified\nassertions. A behavior counts as verified only when a command was run\nand its output shows the expected result; otherwise it MUST be labeled\nan unverified assumption. Test evidence MUST cite the command and the\nobserved outcome (pass/fail counts or concrete output), never a bare\nparaphrase.\n\nRationale: in an autonomous workflow, unmarked assumptions become silent\nregressions.\n\n### IV. Simple Scoped Implementations\n\nImplementations MUST be minimal and scoped to the stated requirement.\nPrefer the smallest change that satisfies the acceptance criteria; do\nnot add configuration, abstraction layers, or speculative features the\ncriteria do not demand. Added complexity MUST be justified against a\nspecific criterion, not anticipated need.\n\nRationale: small, scoped changes are easier to verify and less likely to\nviolate Principle I.\n\n### V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\n\nUnresolved assumptions, open questions, and any behavior that regressed\nor was intentionally changed MUST be written down in project notes\n(HANDOFF.md or the feature spec) with the date and evidence status\n(verified/unverified). Deferred candidate requirements (for example, the\n2026-09-21 put-recency claim variant) MUST be tracked as deferred\nintents, not silently dropped or silently adopted.\n\nRationale: later phases and reviewers need a complete, auditable record\nof what was assumed, deferred, and changed.\n\n## Scope and Deferred Intents\n\nThe constitution governs process only; it does not authorize\nimplementation. The TaggedCache feature (R01-R03) and the Claim-A\ncandidate extension (put recency refresh, variant\nput_no_recency_refresh, 2026-09-21) are deferred to later Spec Kit\nphases (specify, plan, implement). Upstream tests MUST remain unchanged;\nproject-owned tests and notes (for example HANDOFF.md) MAY be added.\n\n## Development Workflow\n\nWork proceeds through the Spec Kit phases (constitution, specify, plan,\nimplement, converge) with artifacts under the specs directory and the\n.specify directory. Each phase MUST close with a summary that cites the\nartifacts it produced and the commands it ran. Convergence MUST rerun\npublic acceptance (acceptance_public.py) and project tests and state any\nunresolved gaps explicitly.\n\n## Governance\n\nThis constitution supersedes conflicting local practices. Amendments\nMUST edit this file, bump the Version per semantic versioning (MAJOR:\nprinciple removed or redefined; MINOR: principle or section added or\nmaterially expanded; PATCH: wording or clarification), update Last\nAmended to the ISO amendment date, and record the change in a Sync\nImpact Report for review. Compliance is reviewed at each phase closing:\nevidence of compliance (test runs, preserved APIs, documented\nassumptions) MUST accompany the phase summary. The Ratified date records\noriginal adoption and is not changed by amendments.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-10-17 | **Last Amended**: 2026-10-17\n"}